          data-ext=".mp4" 
          data-multi="false"
          data-trans="cs_u1_s1_p3_cyber_crime undefined">
          <source src="https://kpcontent.blob.core.windows.net/$web/resources/v2l/720/cs_u1_s1_p3_cyber_crime.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          <track default label="English" kind="captions" srclang="en" src="~/videos/captions/vtt/cs_u1_s1_p3_cyber_crime.vtt">
          <p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos</p>
        </video>
      </div>
      
          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Abraham:</strong> Hello and welcome to our course on Cyber security.</p>
<p>My name’s Abraham</p>
<p><strong>Nicole:</strong> And I’m Nicole</p>
<p>We’ll be with you along the way as you progress through this course.</p>
<p><strong>Abraham:</strong> So, let’s begin shall we.</p>
<p>What exactly is Cyber crime?</p>
<p><strong>Nicole:</strong> Well, cyber crime which can also be known as computer crime, is the use of a computer or other digital device and the internet to commit illegal acts that may affect private individuals, businesses, organisations and governments and can threaten the overall security of the world.</p>
<p><strong>Abraham:</strong> The use of new technologies and the internet has given criminals a new tool for committing crime which can subsequently take place 'virtually' anywhere in the world. Cyber crime is increasing all the time and is becoming more complex affecting essential services, companies and individuals whilst also threatening national security.</p>
<p><strong>Nicole:</strong> Trying to cope with the effects of cyber crime costs the UK billions of pounds each year. The nature of cyber crime is that it's not limited to a specific location and cyber criminals can be based and commit their crimes anywhere, making it difficult for the police and security services to trace. However, cyber criminals do often leave clues to their identity and location and can be traced by skilled cyber crime trackers.</p>
<p><strong>Abraham:</strong> The same skills used by the cyber criminals can also be used by the police and security services to find them. Additionally, even if the criminal is traced, if they are located in a different part of the world, geopolitical issues can mean it’s impossible or not worth the effort to bring them to justice. It’s for these reasons there’s been a huge increase of cyber crime, because for the criminal there is the potential of a high reward with little risk.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
